A||||11||fierodave||Paypal users should read this info||||13||
Z||000000||fierodave||12-29-2001||10:32 AM||||<BR>Hello all,<BR>I wanted to pass along this info to you. Do with it what you want. <P>I have had a long battle with Paypal for money owed to me, and I don't want to see you get burned like I did.<BR>check out this link<BR> <A HREF="http://www.paypalwarning.com/Default.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.paypalwarning.com/Default.htm</A> <P>MAKE sure you don't have a checking account or credit card tied to another accountin your bank, or you could end up with money gone from your other accounts as well.<BR>Make sure your bank contacts you if Paypal wants to do any wire tranfers from any accounts you have.  CALL YOUR BANK ASAP!<BR>Just wanted to share this info with you<BR>Please make sure you read the info at this link if you are SELLER or a BUYER with Paypal.com<BR> <A HREF="http://www.paypalwarning.com/Default.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.paypalwarning.com/Default.htm</A> <P>FD||||reg||13
Z||000001||TRiAD||12-29-2001||10:41 AM||||<I>"Additionally, regulatory authorities in four states (California, New York, Idaho and Louisiana) are investigating whether PayPal, Inc. is engaged in a banking business because of their customers' ability to retain a balance for future transfers. Because Paypal is not licensed as a bank, they are not permitted to engage in a banking business! (Source, IPO Prospectus)  This could spell REAL trouble for anyone with funds "deposited" in Paypal.com!."</I><P>Uh, glad I don't have a paypal account! <BR>Doesn't look like I'll be getting one anytime soon, either. <P>Sorry for your troubles, thanks for being a harbinger for the rest of us. <BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://centralillinoisimports.org/uploads/files/SigRear4.gif">  <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||12-29-2001||11:31 AM||||Wonderful.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>Thanks for sharing.<P>I almost opened a Paypal account several months ago, but changed my mind. <BR>Just had a feeling...<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||12-29-2001||12:01 PM||||Thanks!  I just removed our CC's from it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierodave||12-29-2001||01:53 PM||||I usually don't post info like this because you can't tell what is real or not sometimes on the internet.<BR>but it happened to me and I am a believer<BR>people should be warned about them.<P>It may or may not happen to you. <BR>but after two replys from paypal when they thought I wanted to sign up again, and then I cornered them on the money they stole from my account,  they have no more reply to me. calls to them in Ca gets about the same amount of contact.  <P>once I tell them my name they hang up. or say have your attorney call them!<P>If you have a Paypal account you could be fine, but are you willing to chance your money in other accounts if they are in trouble.  <P>If you know anyone that has a paypal account you may want to send this link to them so they have a chance to decide if it's worth the risk.<P>BTW  this is the reason I do not use Paypal any more.  They are crooks as far as I am concerned.<BR>FD||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||12-29-2001||05:43 PM||||I have real issues with them over exchange rates. They rip me off blindly and claim they are using current rates. The rates they use cost me a lot of money. So much so that I will not use them anymore.<BR>I emailed them a few times about this but all I kept getting back was a claim they used current rates. Claim being the only word fit.<P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero5.gif">         <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000006||BAM-BAM||12-29-2001||06:01 PM||||Found this on the PayPal site.<P>Protection Policies - Traveler's Insurance <P> Is my PayPal account insured?<P> Yes. Through Travelers Insurance, you are protected against unauthorized withdrawals from your PayPal account, including unauthorized withdrawals from any bank account you may have linked to PayPal, up to $100,000.  <P>Just thought I'd add this. Not sure if it's useful or not<P>Peace, B2 OUT! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000007||FieroBUZZ||12-29-2001||06:02 PM||||Looked at PayPal when dealing for some parts. Didn't like what I saw and what they expected from me. Especially from those of us outside of the USA.  Said NO THANKS! Looks like it was the right thing to do.<BR>Gary||||reg||13
Z||000008||chester||12-29-2001||07:41 PM||||Well I've used paypal for about 3 years now and have NEVER had a problem.  Every time I needed to call them I got a LIVE person. I use my account alot.  Maybe I've just been lucky but my experience has been good.<P>Rob D.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">       <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000009||87fastback||12-29-2001||08:23 PM||||I have also ben a member of Paypal for almost 2 years and have only had one minor problem,which they reversed after one short e-mail to them.  Not to say others have not had the same luck, I can only speak from my own experiences.  I do think they charge way too much for business accounts.  Now I think I should have just stayed with a regular account.<P>Regards,<BR>Brent<BR>||||reg||1
